# ssh-keygen -Y verify -f (see "ALLOWED SIGNERS" in ssh-keygen(1)).
# docs/verifying-releases.md says how to use this file. A retired key is removed;
# an older release verifies against this file as it was at that release's tag.
# A key added for releases made through the broker uses the identity
# warden-release, which is what scripts/sign-release.sh and
# docs/verifying-releases.md check against. The older line below keeps its own
# identity and verifies the releases signed before that.
